  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law and the general business law, in\nrelation to requiring the release of individuals from utility, phone and\ntelevision contracts in instances of domestic violence; and to amend a chapter\nof the laws of 2022 amending the public service law and the general business\nlaw relating to requiring the release of individuals from utility, phone and\ntelevision contracts in instances of domestic violence, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S.7157-A and A.6207-B, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S1344",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1344-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§48-a & 91, Pub Serv L; amd §§399-cccc, 399-yy & 399-yyy, Gen Bus L; amd §6, Chap of 2022 (as proposed in S.7157-A & A.6207-B)",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1344\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law and the general business law, in\nrelation to requiring the release of individuals from utility, phone and\ntelevision contracts in instances of domestic violence; and to amend a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the public service law and the\ngeneral business law relating to requiring the release of individuals\nfrom utility, phone and television contracts in instances of domestic\nviolence, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.7157-A and\nA.6207-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.578, to clarify the attestation in writing standard.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by clarifying what a\nvictim of domestic violence must include in the attestation in writing\nto be released from a utility contract; and amends the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 22 of the laws of 2022, this legislation is a\nnegotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to chapter 578 of the Laws of 2022. S.7157A and\nA.6207B both passed the Senate and Assembly.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the public service law and the\ngeneral business law relating to requiring the release of individuals\nfrom utility, phone and television contracts in instances of domestic\nviolence, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 7157-A and A.\n6207-B, takes effect.\n",
